<node id="&quot;TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial obligations imposed on the Recipient as a result of jurisdictional connections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liens for Taxes not yet delinquent or which are being contested in good faith and by appropriate proceedings diligently conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pay and discharge all Taxes upon it or its properties or assets that would reasonably be expected to result in a Material Adverse Effect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payments Free of Taxes; Obligation to Withhold; Payments on Account of Taxes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section addressing tax obligations relevant to the parties involved in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Taxes are governed exclusively by Section 3.01 and are not affected by Section 3.04 regarding increased costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Various forms of taxation that arise under specific jurisdictions, applicable to recipients or entities involved in financial agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"any Taxes from any payment that may be withheld or deducted by the Borrower or the Administrative Agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"as soon as practicable after any payment of Taxes by any Borrower or by the Administrative Agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"means all present or future taxes, levies, imposts, duties, deductions, withholdings imposed by any Governmental Authority."&lt;SEP&gt;"nothing in this Section 2.10 shall affect the rights of any Borrower to withhold for Taxes as provided in Section 3.01."&lt;SEP&gt;"refund of Taxes withheld or deducted from funds paid for the account of such Lender."&lt;SEP&gt;"this Section 11.04(b) shall not apply with respect to Taxes, other than any Taxes that represent Liabilities or related expenses."</data>
