<node id="&quot;AGGREGATE COMMITMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Aggregate Commitments refer to the total amount of commitments made by Lenders under the loan agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"All obligations of the Borrowers shall survive termination of the Aggregate Commitments, repayment of all Obligations hereunder and resignation of the Administrative Agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Company may, upon notice to the Administrative Agent, terminate the Aggregate Commitments, or from time to time permanently reduce the Aggregate Commitments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The aggregate amount of the Commitments subject to such reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The date of termination of the Aggregate Commitments pursuant to Section 2.04 or 8.02."&lt;SEP&gt;"The termination of the Aggregate Commitments and the repayment, satisfaction or discharge of all the Obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The total amount of commitments available to the Borrowers from the Lenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"commitment fee in US Dollars equal to the Applicable Rate times the actual daily amount by which the Aggregate Commitments exceed the Total Outstandings."&lt;SEP&gt;"means, at any time, the Commitments of all the Lenders at such time. As of the Closing Date, the Aggregate Commitments equal to US$15,000,000,000."&lt;SEP&gt;"the Total Outstandings at such time exceed an amount equal to 105% of the Aggregate Commitments then in effect."&lt;SEP&gt;"the total sum of commitments by various lenders in relation to the agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b637d0405cd4cb720fa5cc51c6eae36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a26a8f2185f90f4a7c53bd3079e8fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682c5ead894d7b0b1048fdd5c656db16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f21272229c5dd2ca4ee5799336e5131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ff0231dce6b36c6d76b94f8cf52da74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afd4f755e720f4d83553494467fe767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65b1b045a2cc5774bf77945831da1f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47d7e61b5ba03e84e04debff056fcb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0264408b13fa227639776ebb2dea19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6ea716059b2dcd9fb31d7b464c8ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5e7a44196120f6da0565ee30ce4f44c</data>
