  <data key="d0">"FACILITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Term Benchmark Loan is a type of borrowing that can involve continuation or conversion under specified conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial product whose interest rate is linked to a specified benchmark rate, involving various currencies as described."&lt;SEP&gt;"A loan that is tied to a benchmark interest rate over a defined term period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any prepayment of a Term Benchmark Loan or RFR Loan shall be accompanied by all accrued interest on the amount prepaid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Term Benchmark Loans are loans made under specific market rates such as Term SOFR or EURIBO Rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"a type of loan whose interest rate is tied to a benchmark rate over a term period."&lt;SEP&gt;"continuation, conversion, payment or prepayment of any Term Benchmark Loan on a day other than the last day of the Interest Period for such Loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"disbursed or converted to or continued as a Term Benchmark Loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"means a Term SOFR Loan, an ABBR Loan, a CDOR Loan, a Term CORRA Loan, a EURIBOR Loan or a TIBOR Loan."</data>
