  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GAAP applies on a consistent basis for the preparation of financial data submitted pursuant to the Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"GAAP refers to Generally Accepted Accounting Principles that are used for financial reporting. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Generally Accepted Accounting Principles under which the Company's financial statements should be prepared."&lt;SEP&gt;"Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, the accounting framework used for financial reporting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, the accounting standard that governs how financial statements are prepared and obligations reported."&lt;SEP&gt;"Generally accepted accounting principles in the United States as defined in the Accounting Standards Codification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prepared in accordance with GAAP, subject only to normal year-end audit adjustments."</data>
