  <data key="d0">"BASE RATE BENCHMARK"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A benchmark for U.S. Dollar term loans as established by the CME Term SOFR Administrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of term rate that may be considered when determining the Benchmark."&lt;SEP&gt;"Each Term SOFR Borrowing shall bear interest on the outstanding principal amount thereof for the Interest Period applicable to such Borrowing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Term SOFR is a secured overnight financing rate used as a reference for Term Benchmark Loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Term SOFR, the EURIBO Rate, the TIBO Rate, the CDO Rate or the AUD Bank Bill Rate for the applicable Agreed Currency."&lt;SEP&gt;"The interest rate on Base Rate Loans determined by reference to Term SOFR component of the Base Rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rate based on SOFR used to determine interest rates for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"if such Benchmark is Term SOFR, 5:00 a.m., Chicago time, on the day that is two U.S. Government Securities Business Days preceding the date of such setting."&lt;SEP&gt;"refers to the Secured Overnight Financing Rate that is used as a benchmark for loans and borrowing."&lt;SEP&gt;"the Benchmark Replacement with respect to Term SOFR."&lt;SEP&gt;"the Term SOFR for a one month Interest Period as published two U.S. Government Securities Business Days prior to such day."</data>
