<node id="&quot;BENCHMARK REPLACEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"'Benchmark Replacement' means, for any Available Tenor."&lt;SEP&gt;"A substitute mechanism for the existing benchmark pertaining to various currencies, as outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"As per the loan document, if a benchmark is determined to be non-representative, a Benchmark Replacement will be implemented."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benchmark Replacement defines the alternative rate that replaces the original benchmark rate when necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benchmark Replacement is discussed with respect to Loans denominated in US Dollars and Euro."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conditions under which a Benchmark Replacement is determined and applied to Loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Benchmark Replacement is a term used to denote the new benchmark that replaces the current benchmark in loan agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Benchmark Replacement refers to any alternative interest rate used in the event of a Benchmark Transition Event."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alternative benchmark rate that is applied when the original benchmark is deemed ineffective or non-representative."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alternative benchmark that replaces the then-current Benchmark for Canadian Dollars."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a mechanism outlined in the agreement allowing for changes in the reference rate used in the loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"bearing interest at the Benchmark Replacement described in clause (2)(a) of the definition of such term for the respective Available Tenor."</data>
