<node id="&quot;BENCHMARK TRANSITION EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A 'Benchmark Transition Event' occurs if a public statement or publication of information indicates that the then-current Benchmark is no longer representative."&lt;SEP&gt;"A 'Benchmark Transition Event' refers to market conditions that necessitate a change in the Benchmark Rate used for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Benchmark Transition Event is an occurrence that provides a mechanism for determining an alternative interest rate due to changes in the benchmark."&lt;SEP&gt;"An event that triggers the need for a Benchmark Replacement as outlined in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benchmark Transition Event refers to a specific scenario when a shift occurs from one benchmark to another pertaining to interest rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Defined events that trigger the need for a Benchmark Replacement Date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Events that trigger changes in Benchmark Rates and Loans accordingly."&lt;SEP&gt;"an event that triggers changes in the reference rate used for interest calculations in loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"“Benchmark Transition Event” refers to the occurrence of specific events regarding the Benchmark, such as the administrator ceasing to provide Available Tenors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e27d526ebea615c4be84a55d4f0b816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-222ae97c7f771b1a3946c9792829f5c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd223e171341ca9ee826596f361fff2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb02eac2287146277b8109a81d8e8163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f7e377923354fdd272fea5619419e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac3eabdef973ef98caa3f06b7973c3ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edbaf061a5d10dddff589ed1a422c891&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170b99e108ab1f8946426f5753c65c25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8d92840a114cf25e84b01ae67d626e</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-6651d386274d94a69cbc67e7a7e06bb2</data>
