<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A company owned or controlled by another company, referred to as the parent or holding company."&lt;SEP&gt;"A corporation, partnership, joint venture, limited liability company or other business entity of which a majority of the shares or interests are beneficially owned or controlled."&lt;SEP&gt;"All references herein to a 'Subsidiary' or to 'Subsidiaries' shall refer to a Subsidiary or Subsidiaries of the Company."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any Subsidiary of the Company that may also engage in commercial lending activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any Subsidiary relating to the Company or any of their respective businesses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any company owned or controlled by the primary Company that may be involved in the financial agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Applicable entities that are part of the corporate structure of the Company."&lt;SEP&gt;"Each Borrower and each Subsidiary thereof is in compliance in all material respects with the requirements of all Laws and all orders, writs, injunctions, and decrees applicable to it or to its properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Each Subsidiary of the Company that is or becomes a Designated Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indebtedness of the Company or any Subsidiary in an aggregate outstanding principal amount of $1,500,000,000 or more."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a Subsidiary of the Company involved in financial or asset transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsidiary as referenced in the context indicating its connection to the Company and the ordinary conduct of business."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subsidiary or other Affiliate may engage in business with the Administrative Agent under the terms of the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"any Subsidiary or Affiliate thereof"</data>
