</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BORROWER"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "Borrowers" refers to entities or individuals that receive loans from Lenders, as defined in the relevant loan documents and agreements. The Borrowers, which may include specific designated borrowers such as the Company, have various obligations under Article III of the agreements, including surviving the termination of Aggregate Commitments, the repayment of all Obligations, and the resignation of the Administrative Agent. Each Borrower is severally responsible for making payments as required by the agreements and for indemnifying the Administrative Agent, as well as other recipients involved in the transactions.

Borrowers are required to pay interest at the Default Rate unless otherwise waived by the Required Lenders. They must maintain accurate records, with any mistakes in recording not limiting their obligations to pay any outstanding amounts. Furthermore, Borrowers are tasked with developing and maintaining policies that ensure compliance with applicable laws.

In scenarios involving erroneous payments or alterations to contact details, each Borrower is required to address these issues cooperatively. They are also expected to prepay loans denominated in Alternative Currencies as necessary to manage their outstanding amounts and ensure compliance with terms outlined in the agreements. Overall, the Borrowers are integral to the financial transactions facilitated by the Lenders, and their roles are governed by the terms specified in the contract documents.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e27d526ebea615c4be84a55d4f0b816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf4af83bed6de952eac63d1c88a41b05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbdf531655886df91c6a944df9d3f8b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b73f1653519cb5388ba4815ea4c08f2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ed9aefdad35a1c17af0afe893bb8783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb5948dc7921697af24df64c845c94cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd320686a1f984b7fbe703eddfa1995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26824d3e5b8a3855832d86ede39df399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ff0231dce6b36c6d76b94f8cf52da74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d68df312f7f16c4d8e4af5e1d769f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7720be909cc189d41144f4a242562dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b637d0405cd4cb720fa5cc51c6eae36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf8265680b576d949a33956718f4bea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47d7e61b5ba03e84e04debff056fcb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e904b36bc25f49cd076d9e998971fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c914ecc1ba4cc04797717a927d91fd0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a7fc07faff35fcf2b53abfe1e576bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54326f4acdff2aa7b9cbed3bcfd85041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac3eabdef973ef98caa3f06b7973c3ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402c64da04ddc5608cee1856dcbb9a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6ea716059b2dcd9fb31d7b464c8ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6867baaac8b80330e888c5f64e303ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f778cd58ca4cfdb5bd37891a04aa6c8</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-6651d386274d94a69cbc67e7a7e06bb2</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-amazon</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SCHEDULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "Interest Period" refers to a defined duration applicable to the interest rate on loans, particularly in the context of Term Benchmark Loans. It encompasses several key aspects, including the length of time the interest rate remains fixed or variable before any adjustments or renewals occur. Interest Periods are crucial for determining when interest will be calculated or due for a loan and establish the timeframe within which interest accrues for each borrowing.

Specifically, the Interest Period specifies the duration for which the applicable interest rate is set, impacting the calculations associated with loans denominated in various currencies, including alternative currencies. Additionally, it governs the processes required for borrowing, such as the necessary consent of all lenders before a Term Benchmark Loan is finalized.

Typically, an Interest Period may last for a month or other specified timeframes, and if an Interest Period concludes on a day that is not a Business Day, it is extended to the next succeeding Business Day. Overall, the Interest Period is essential for accurate interest rate calculations, borrower obligations, and maintaining consistency in loan agreements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-136369fb607ffcc8874842ebfb8e0494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-114048bd63b08e08234db8c9890cd85e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c2f465958aa8d827747f82da9775636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6591c56671bab439c19567c096b29261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76721ac2a3b4759d7a2bf2bc4ad4ef87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d58db72e1791e0d73773cc0befded1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d76442dc7c26385612da21161d48e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65b1b045a2cc5774bf77945831da1f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e63704c823f60ff60db1c6d5c81360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0c6db4a22086f6817a75820f943bae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe20bb927a839907621def342fe8ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb02eac2287146277b8109a81d8e8163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d90f9159b8174053b0f23f53399fd87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4fe896846cd167076f22c0725da64e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab70c1cf5fa53da3db1e0969d425127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69954b308816d8f15f00d6a218095eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1de73b3018151cf03fd33ccbe0fd5885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682c5ead894d7b0b1048fdd5c656db16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf8265680b576d949a33956718f4bea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013593d672f130ddc9fe444ebd690c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8d92840a114cf25e84b01ae67d626e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec07a1eab7686ab6eef9aa9d7515a3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c30c831ae2ececd9089c39cf051b149e</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-6651d386274d94a69cbc67e7a7e06bb2</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-amazon</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">LENDER refers to an individual or entity that provides loans, including both the principal amount and interest, to Borrowers under specified agreements. These entities play a crucial role in financing by delivering funds as outlined in the Loan Documents, with the expectation of repayment, usually with interest. Each Lender operates under terms detailed in the credit agreement and is engaged in making, acquiring, or holding commercial loans.

In the context of their operations, Lenders maintain a direct relationship with the Borrowers and the Administrative Agent, responsible for payments, communications, and various determinations. They have the right to assign or pledge their rights and obligations under the agreement and must notify the Administrative Agent of any changes in their contact information. Each Lender is also responsible for notifying the Administrative Agent and the other Lenders in case of defaults or relevant alterations in loan agreements.

All Lenders are subject to specific conditions regarding costs and expenses related to changes in law affecting their liquidity or capital requirements. They may also request necessary documentation from Borrowers to ensure compliance with payment regulations. In circumstances where a Lender becomes a Defaulting Lender, certain provisions come into play until the situation is remedied.

The term "Lender" encompasses various types of financial institutions or individuals involved in lending, facilitating transactions, and providing loans, all under the framework specified in the respective agreements. Each Lender is expected to manage its proportionate share of the total credit exposure and may receive payments distributed based on its applicable percentage. Their actions and responsibilities are further guided by regulations established in the agreements, ensuring collaboration and notification between all involved parties.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e27d526ebea615c4be84a55d4f0b816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6482914c0025ca6e6f96599e51f700a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-231a0d0a9307dfd95b4523972c93623b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bd69db9f06963e7195b77c581e5be64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbdf531655886df91c6a944df9d3f8b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76721ac2a3b4759d7a2bf2bc4ad4ef87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d58db72e1791e0d73773cc0befded1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f21272229c5dd2ca4ee5799336e5131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb201d631d7848d67d10aae35e099b65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1eb67ffcaf5d2d9cf2ad7c51a9e64eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6dda991dc457e11db2c6f0fe242fa41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46b17dc38cedefc3b1d4ee3fb0408407&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a1007905a86e506e6e4f88af978a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a27f77c73892a85827ba609cc034cc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787299885ac70dd86e4f90a80cc13d8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b55e21aa490b434d07102ac0a0f431fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acdc38292651612aba76cd6c268e569c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ed9aefdad35a1c17af0afe893bb8783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93e512310577a496a30e98195826f58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd240b40422f73cdf615b12afee971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0c6db4a22086f6817a75820f943bae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ca8b0468db8545a24275a4dfce981f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa8c3d4e7bd2cf291921773f12fdecb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d019c3df8aed44c5ff8ea4da836ddf9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb5948dc7921697af24df64c845c94cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8282e1ae265a3d7d81c2a8812fb723aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26824d3e5b8a3855832d86ede39df399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7dcabb468b7608dfc9bd9ddc9d5a8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f1e764a2d3e36453f112d7fa49a7bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ff0231dce6b36c6d76b94f8cf52da74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afd4f755e720f4d83553494467fe767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d68df312f7f16c4d8e4af5e1d769f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3480d75b314bdfade2362555e7d58a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29f4c749687effde35d0fcb513406dfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9200500d9e9bba8db3c46d21566903a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c12e211d90e41dfed2685959712c895&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-decc7f4374f137eff5fab6d32d23ffb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64b92c3143192c5d21c6bc4366d17ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5e7a44196120f6da0565ee30ce4f44c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7720be909cc189d41144f4a242562dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19647c660eda6fb81