<node id="&quot;OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "Obligations" encompasses a wide range of financial and contractual responsibilities that Borrowers and Lenders must fulfill under various agreements, notably Loan Documents. It includes all debts, liabilities, covenants, and duties that Borrowers must adhere to, as well as any payments due in connection with these obligations, which must be paid in full in cash. The financial responsibilities associated with the Obligations are critical, as they relate to the commitments established in the contractual agreements between the parties involved.

The Obligations specifically refer to the duties of the Borrowers under the loan agreement, including any and all payments made by or on account of their obligations. Moreover, it is noted that the Lender’s obligations under the agreement remain unchanged, suggesting a consistent expectation regarding the financial commitments. These Obligations survive various changes such as the resignation of the Administrative Agent or the replacement of any Lender, highlighting their significance even in shifting circumstances.

Further, the obligations of Designated Borrowers are guaranteed by the Company as articulated in the relevant Guaranty, ensuring that these financial responsibilities are upheld. They encompass all forms of responsibilities, including the duty to pay amounts owed, and outline the rights of Lenders, including their ability to vote on claims in proceedings affecting their interests.

Overall, the concept of Obligations serves as a comprehensive framework for understanding the financial duties that both Borrowers and Lenders are bound to uphold in accordance with the stipulated terms, including any accrued and unpaid interest on loans, as well as the implications of erroneous payments that do not satisfy these obligations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bd69db9f06963e7195b77c581e5be64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf4af83bed6de952eac63d1c88a41b05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f21272229c5dd2ca4ee5799336e5131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1eb67ffcaf5d2d9cf2ad7c51a9e64eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a1007905a86e506e6e4f88af978a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b73f1653519cb5388ba4815ea4c08f2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f72e9f7fa7f94e8348291ef7c5f0bdef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93e512310577a496a30e98195826f58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb5948dc7921697af24df64c845c94cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7dcabb468b7608dfc9bd9ddc9d5a8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c12e211d90e41dfed2685959712c895&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5e7a44196120f6da0565ee30ce4f44c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-656cbd22be80eec811fc0e6c4285e66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a7fc07faff35fcf2b53abfe1e576bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60b528159be4d1e030e14d2840fd1dd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3d28f90b238b652e176c2dd580a5570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ebc127d2ee310e0ffab541e513e3c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e137338a832bcfa1152a34534e03e73f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402c64da04ddc5608cee1856dcbb9a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47f6528050492ac38aa96576c8e318f</data>
