<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Administrative Agent" refers to Citibank, N.A. in its role as the administrative agent under the Loan Documents. This entity is appointed to act on behalf of the lenders in a loan agreement, facilitating the management of the loan process and serving as the primary communication link between lenders and borrowers. 

The Administrative Agent is responsible for overseeing the administration of loan agreements, ensuring compliance with the terms stipulated in the agreements, and managing various aspects of financial transactions. This includes managing communications regarding liabilities, payments, and transactions, and exercising designated powers as outlined in the loan documents.

In addition to facilitating communication, the Administrative Agent holds a supervisory role, with the discretion to modify interest periods related to benchmarks. It plays a crucial role in the syndication of credit facilities and is authorized to notify lenders about requests, ensure they receive necessary documents, and oversee the execution of various administrative tasks associated with the loans.

Key responsibilities of the Administrative Agent include overseeing the obligations and actions of all parties involved, administering the loan agreements, ensuring compliance matters for both the Company and the lenders, and managing the relationship between lenders and borrowers. The agent is also empowered to obtain required resolutions, certificates, and legal opinions for loan agreements while also addressing any issues related to Defaulting Lenders.

Additionally, the Administrative Agent has the authority to manage the assignment of rights and obligations during defaults, oversee borrowing notices, and handle currency-related transactions under alternative currencies. It operates with a commercial motivation, without interests in the general performance or operations of the Company or any of its subsidiaries.

Ultimately, the Administrative Agent acts as a non-fiduciary agent for the borrowers and has a critical role in the efficient administration and enforcement of loan agreements and related obligations, ensuring that all procedural expectations and</data>
