<edge source="&quot;LENDERS&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">127.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The "ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT" and "LENDERS" operate in a collaborative capacity within the framework of loan agreements. The Administrative Agent represents the interests of the Lenders, ensuring their rights are upheld and facilitating communication between the Lenders and the Company. Each Lender is obligated to pay any unpaid amounts to the Administrative Agent, which acts on behalf of all Lenders to manage the Loans and enforce rights in accordance with the agreement.

The Administrative Agent plays a pivotal role in coordinating activities among the Lenders, streamlining the execution of Loans and Commitments. They are responsible for notifying the Lenders about critical updates, including changes to interest rates, Aggregate Commitments, and any amendments to the loan agreements. Additionally, the Administrative Agent delivers Term CORRA Notices to the Lenders and informs them of any changes to the status of the Designated Borrower, including terminations.

In the context of loan syndication, the Administrative Agent organizes the process for the Lenders providing credit facilities and represents them in decisions related to Benchmark Replacement and other agreement modifications. Furthermore, the Administrative Agent may take specific actions with the consent of the Required Lenders, demonstrating an ongoing collaborative relationship while managing all Loan Documents and necessary amendments. Ultimately, the relationship between the Administrative Agent and the Lenders is centered on mutual compliance and facilitation of the loan agreements.</data>
