<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d5">130.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the Borrower and the Lender is defined by a monetary transaction in which the Lender provides funds to the Borrower. In this process, the Borrower is obligated to repay the loan under the terms specified in the loan agreements, also referred to as Loan Documents. The Lender makes requests to the Borrower, often facilitated through the Administrative Agent, which involves communication regarding the Borrower's obligations.

Each Borrower is required to execute and deliver a Note to the Lender upon request, which formalizes the lender-borrower relationship. The Lender's provision of loans establishes a fundamental obligor-lender relationship, where the Borrower is recognized as the entity responsible for the repayment of the funds received, typically along with interest as established in their agreement. Additionally, Lenders are notified of essential details related to these loans and can exercise certain rights against the Borrower as a direct creditor if needed.

In cases where the Borrower is identified as a U.S. Person, there are specific expectations for Lenders who are also U.S. Persons, including the delivery of certain communications to the Company. Overall, the Borrower engages with the Lender under the established terms of the Agreement and is responsible for fulfilling repayment obligations as outlined in the loan agreements.</data>
  <data key="d7">"Borrower-Lender"&lt;SEP&gt;"Creditor Relationship"&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Transaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"Lending Relationship"&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Agreement"&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Provision"&lt;SEP&gt;"Obligation"&lt;SEP&gt;"Obligation, Communications"&lt;SEP&gt;"Transaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"engagement, financing"&lt;SEP&gt;"loan relationship"&lt;SEP&gt;"obligation"&lt;SEP&gt;5&lt;SEP&gt;Financial Loan Relationship&lt;SEP&gt;Financial Transaction&lt;</data>
