  <data key="d9">DOC-6651d386274d94a69cbc67e7a7e06bb2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">121.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the "ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT" and the "BORROWER" is defined by a series of roles and responsibilities that facilitate loan agreements and transactions. The Administrative Agent acts on behalf of the Lender, coordinating dealings with the Borrower and managing the overall communication regarding loan agreements. This includes delivering notices about determinations made by the Lender to the Borrower and ensuring that the Borrower complies with the terms of the loan agreement.

The Administrative Agent is responsible for withholding or making deductions based on the information received from the Borrower and overseeing the management of the Borrower's obligations. Each Borrower is required to represent and warrant to the Administrative Agent and Lenders that they are duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing. Furthermore, the Administrative Agent engages in various business activities with the Borrower, showing a professional relationship in the lending context.

The Administrative Agent facilitates interactions between the Borrowers and Lenders, ensuring that payments are made according to the agreements in place. This includes managing loan transactions, making funds available to the Borrower, and overseeing the compliance of Borrower obligations. Additionally, the Administrative Agent plays a significant role in allowing Borrowers to prepay affected loans under specific conditions and communicates conditions regarding loan commitments and prepayments.

The Borrower is expected to take specific actions as dictated by the Administrative Agent's notices, particularly in relation to prepayments and loan requests. To initiate prepayments or make loan requests, the Borrower must provide an irrevocable notice to the Administrative Agent. Overall, the entities maintain a structured and professional interaction centered on facilitating smooth loan operations and compliance with agreements.</data>
