<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">276.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Administrative Agent serves a pivotal role on behalf of the Lender, functioning as an intermediary in the administration and management of loans and related agreements. This includes a variety of responsibilities such as assisting with tax assessments and liabilities, overseeing compliance with funding obligations, and facilitating communication between the Lender and borrowers, as well as among multiple Lenders.

The Administrative Agent is authorized by each Lender to manage loan transactions, enforce terms of agreements, and handle documentation requests. This includes notifying Lenders about changes in contact information, wire instructions, loan notices, and fund disbursement. The Agent ensures that payments are distributed to each Lender based on their applicable percentage and coordinates actions prior to the closing date.

In all transactions, the Administrative Agent acts on behalf of the Lenders, handling their interests in transactions and ensuring that indemnification payments are processed according to agreement requirements. The Agent's rights and duties are constrained to the framework of the agreements made with the Lenders, which means any modifications require consent from them.

Additionally, the Administrative Agent has the authority to notify Lenders of critical occurrences, such as when a Lender is identified as a Defaulting Lender or when there are erroneous payments. The relationship between the Administrative Agent and the Lender is essential for the successful administration of loans and commitments, emphasizing the close operational relationship and the functional management of the entire loan process.</data>
