<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d5">109.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the COMPANY and the LENDER is defined by a set of agreements and obligations that govern their interactions. Any Lender that qualifies as a U.S. Person is required to deliver specified documentation to the Company and the Administrative Agent. The Company maintains the right to replace a Lender if that Lender falls under certain categories, such as a Defaulting Lender, Non-Extending Lender, or Non-Consenting Lender. 

Each Lender is obliged to update their certification and inform the Company of any inability to do so, ensuring that communication remains effective. Furthermore, Lenders can notify the Company of any changes in contact details. In the event that a Lender requests compensation under a specific section of their agreement, the Company may also replace that Lender as outlined in another provision.

Lenders have the ability to deliver payment certificates regarding taxes and liabilities, further emphasizing their financial role. The direct lending relationship is established through the communication of obligations and decisions related to loans, and the Company must adhere to the Lender’s agreements in terms of loan repayment and compliance.

The Company is responsible for compensating the Lender for losses incurred, as well as for any reductions stemming from changes affecting capital and liquidity requirements. Additionally, compensation must be provided for costs arising from legal changes that impact the loans. In managing their obligations, the Company must also consider the actions of the Lender, especially in scenarios involving assignments or waivers.

Moreover, the Company is required to notify each Lender of any Defaults that occur and must fulfill its obligations while the Lender holds any Commitment under the agreement. Compensation to the Lenders is structured according to their Applicable Percentage, and the Lender's financial support is crucial for the Company under the</data>
  <data key="d7">"Commitment"&lt;SEP&gt;"Compensation"&lt;SEP&gt;"Extension Procedures"&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Agreement"&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Provision"&lt;SEP&gt;"Notification"&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment Certification"&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment"&lt;SEP&gt;"Replacement"&lt;SEP&gt;"Transaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"Update, Notification"&lt;SEP&gt;"assignment, waiver"&lt;SEP&gt;"compensation"&lt;SEP&gt;"lending relationship"&lt;SEP&gt;communication</data>
  <data key="d8">chunk-231a0d0a9307dfd95b4523972c93623b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbdf531655886df91c6a944df9d3f8b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d58db72e1791e0d73773cc0befded1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1eb67ffcaf5d2d9cf2ad7c51a9e64eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd240b40422f73cdf615b12afee971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8282e1ae265a3d7d81c2a8812fb723aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ff0231dce6b36c6d76b94f8cf52da74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a26a8f2185f90f4a7c53bd3079e8fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf8265680b576d949a33956718f4bea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908e057abb31aea6181bbab412901e6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2878cd0c0d66978fe2fad240129e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e904b36bc25f49cd076d9e998971fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c914ecc1ba4cc04797717a927d91fd0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77b7e5fb7ef25d62c32b6776f5ce5ec9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a5ad517c90fcfe773feaed3aa6ca69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b08b3f3072ce727419bf04e8f76f991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6fb04e696f0e29f406fbbcbc3c61988&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402c64da04ddc5608cee1856dcbb9a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f778cd58ca4cfdb5bd37891a04aa6c8</data>
  <data key="d9">DOC-6651d386274d94a69cbc67e7a7e06bb2</data>
</edge>
